WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:01.669
OK.

00:00:01.669 --> 00:00:02.880
Very exciting.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.320
We have increased the duration of The Daily
Show by 10 percent.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.800
Now, this just might not sound like some big
victory, but a year ago we increased the duration

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.849
of the show 10 percent.

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:12.849
We've done it again.

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:17.090
The way we've done this is by cutting the
amount of breaks from the broadcast show we

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.500
have this hour show on radio TV.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.920
It can't go longer than an hour.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.050
There were commercial radio shows that in
an hour have thirty eight minutes of content

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.330
that used to be us.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.590
We've expanded, expanded, expanded, expanded.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:34.930
We've now added another 10 percent to the
show, making it nearly a full hour show.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.199
And that is fantastic.

00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:40.839
You might have noticed this week that we're
able to look at some stories in more depth.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:42.699
We're not going to cram more into the show.

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:47.879
It's just going to let us do more depth for
the shows, for the stories that we're already

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:48.879
doing.

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:50.479
I think it's a really great thing.

00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:55.300
We are also adding a daily written digest
of the show.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.549
A lot of people have written to me and said,
you know, David, I prefer to read stuff.

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:00.850
I like your perspectives.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:01.850
I like the show.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.070
But it's easier for me to read on the subway.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.740
Imagine when people took the subway to work
in those days.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.049
I like reading on the subway or whatever.

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:12.880
We are going to be turning our daily newsletter
into.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.200
A sort of written digest of the show.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.649
You can sign up for what will become this
in the next couple of weeks on my Web site

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:24.210
at David Pakman dot com, just sign up for
the newsletter.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.329
You'll get all of it.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:26.600
It's all great stuff.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.340
You can also sign up for that at David Pakman
dot sub stack dot com.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.609
It will also provide a new way to support
the show, but it's also going to be free for

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:37.369
everybody that wants it for free.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.619
Really, really great stuff.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:43.590
I am thinking of this virus phase for the
show.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.350
I am thinking of it as the process of a caterpillar
becoming a butterfly.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.350
OK.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.210
I use this analogy on the bonus show yesterday.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:56.159
We were a caterpillar going into Corona virus
during Corona virus.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:58.749
We are in the chrysalis stage.

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:02.759
I'm going back to like third grade science
class.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:05.219
We are now in the chrysalis stage.

00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:11.180
And my goal is that we will come out of Corona
virus reemerging as a butterfly, less orange,

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.280
of course, than a monarch.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.180
I don't want to be like Donald Trump, but
as a butterfly with a lot of great things

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.799
and a better program and all of these things.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:22.220
So exciting stuff and very, very good news.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.870
Looking forward to all of it.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.870
Once we get past this difficult time

